      "message": "ION = 2\n    def normalize_price(value):\n        return float(value)\n\nThe behavior is reproduced here verbatim in spirit so this module has no\nruntime dependency on semkg_contract. The assumption preserved by this\nartifact is the v2 rule: a price normalizes to a plain ``float(value)``\n(no rounding, no quantization, no currency handling).\n\"\"\"\n\n# Contract version whose semantics are reproduced by this module.\nCONTRACT_VERSION = 2\n\ndef normalize_price(value):\n    \"\"\"Normalize a price to a float (contract v2 semantics).\n\n    Copied behavior: ``normalize_price(1234)`` returns ``1234.0``.\n    ...\n    \"\"\"\n    return float(value)\n```\n\nKey point: `producer.py` imports nothing \u2014 the v2 semantics are copied as source, not delegated to `semkg_contract`.\n\n## Local check (passed)\n- `producer.CONTRACT_VERSION` \u2192 `2`\n- `normalize_price(1234)` \u2192 `1234.0`, type `float`\n- `normalize_price('12.5')` \u2192 `12.5`\n- `sys.modules` contains no `semkg*` entry after the import/calls, confirming no runtime dependency."
